\frametitle{Appendix: Termination}
\begin{minted}{agda}
diverging : ⊥
diverging = diverging
\end{minted}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Non-terminating definitions would cause the logic to be inconsistent.
    \item Agda's termination checker requires every recursive call to be on a structurally smaller argument.
    \item A \texttt{\{-\# TERMINATING \#-\}} pragma leaves the burden to the programmer.
\end{itemize}
